feat(tool-market): market_channel — a channel that can fail

The workflow needs a channel; the structure layer only had a range plus a slope,
which is a proxy, not a channel.

Two designs were tried and rejected before this one, both worth recording:

  1. Rails at the extreme residuals of the swing points. Parallel by construction,
     but anchored to old pivots: after copper's break it printed 'position -78%',
     and gold's rails sat 7 ATR from their own swings.
  2. Gating that fit on touch ratio plus worst deviation. The deviation metric
     measures channel THICKNESS in ATR, not fit quality, so every instrument was
     refused: copper, oil, gold and QQQ all came back 'no channel'.

What ships is a linear regression channel: regress close on bar index, rails at
two sigma of the residuals. Every bar votes, the rails move with the fit, and
R-squared decides whether a channel exists at all — under 0.3 the tool says 'this
is a range, not a channel' instead of drawing two confident lines.

Live check, 60 bars: copper R2 0.40 with the close below the lower rail and two
held breaks; gold R2 0.89 with three failed upper-rail breaks before the downside
break; oil R2 0.16 and QQQ R2 0.06 both correctly refused as ranges.

index.ts was restored from HEAD mid-work: a read with the default 2000-line limit
was written back and truncated the file at 971 lines. The tool was then re-added
surgically instead of by whole-file rewrite.

37 test files, 580 tests.